======

This project is a derivative work. It adapts the algorithm and API client of:

    fast-jev-compaction
    https://github.com/tamaratran/fast-jev-compaction
    Copyright (c) Allie Laabs
    Licensed under the MIT License

The upstream source is not vendored in this repository. `setup.sh` clones and
builds it from its own repository, so upstream remains the single source of
truth for the compaction algorithm and cannot go stale inside a fork.

What this repository adds on top of upstream:

  - `hermes-compact.mjs` — an adapter for the Hermes transcript format
    (`role: user | assistant | tool`, tool results as their own messages,
    `tool_calls[].function.arguments` as a JSON string), plus in-place pruning
    of the original messages so that ids, reasoning fields and metadata survive.
  - Windowing for transcripts too large for a single request ("history too large
    for Jev"). Upstream throws; this adapter splits the transcript into windows.
  - The `PROTECTED_TOOLS` policy: state-changing calls are never removed, because
    Jev's judgement is not stable across sessions.
  - `SKILL.md` — the skill that makes the tool available to a Hermes agent.

